{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1605","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. PalindORme"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An integer array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$ is said to be a PalindORme if ($$$a_{1}$$$ $$$|$$$ $$$a_{2} $$$ $$$|$$$ $$$ \\ldots $$$ $$$|$$$ $$$ a_{i}) = (a_{{n - i + 1}} $$$ $$$|$$$ $$$ \\ldots $$$ $$$|$$$ $$$ a_{{n - 1}} $$$ $$$|$$$ $$$ a_{n}) $$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"for all"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$ 1 \\leq i \\leq n$$$, where $$$|$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#OR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise OR operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An integer array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$ is considered to be good if its elements can be rearranged to form a PalindORme. Formally, array $$$a$$$ is good if there exists a permutation $$$p_1, p_2, \\ldots p_n$$$ (an array where each integer from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ appears exactly once) for which $$$a_{p_1}, a_{p_2}, \\ldots a_{p_n}$$$ is a PalindORme."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the number of good arrays of length $$$n$$$, consisting only of integers in the range $$$[0, 2^{k} - 1]$$$, and print it modulo some prime $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two arrays $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ and $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$ are considered to be different if there exists any $$$i$$$ $$$(1 \\leq i \\leq n)$$$ such that $$$a_i \\ne b_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line of the input contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$k$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n,k \\leq 80$$$, $$$10^8 \\lt m \\lt 10^9$$$). It is guaranteed that $$$m$$$ is prime."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer  — the number of good arrays modulo $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 1 998244353\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 2 999999733\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n40\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7 3 796735397\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1871528\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 46 606559127\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n177013\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, both the possible arrays $$$[0]$$$ and $$$[1]$$$ are good."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, some examples of good arrays are:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2, 1, 2]$$$ because it is already PalindORme."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1, 1, 0]$$$ because it can rearranged to $$$[1, 0, 1]$$$ which is PalindORme"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that $$$[1, 1, 0]$$$, $$$[1, 0, 1]$$$ and $$$[0, 1, 1]$$$ are all good arrays and are considered to be different according to the definition in the statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample, an example of a good array is $$$[1, 0, 1, 4, 2, 5, 4]$$$. It can be rearranged to an array $$$b = [1, 5, 0, 2, 4, 4, 1]$$$ which is a PalindORme because:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\mathrm{OR}(1, 1)$$$ = $$$\\mathrm{OR}(7, 7)$$$ = $$$1$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\mathrm{OR}(1, 2)$$$ = $$$\\mathrm{OR}(6, 7)$$$ = $$$5$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\mathrm{OR}(1, 3)$$$ = $$$\\mathrm{OR}(5, 7)$$$ = $$$5$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\mathrm{OR}(1, 4)$$$ = $$$\\mathrm{OR}(4, 7)$$$ = $$$7$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\mathrm{OR}(1, 5)$$$ = $$$\\mathrm{OR}(3, 7)$$$ = $$$7$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\mathrm{OR}(1, 6)$$$ = $$$\\mathrm{OR}(2, 7)$$$ = $$$7$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\mathrm{OR}(1, 7)$$$ = $$$\\mathrm{OR}(1, 7)$$$ = $$$7$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here $$$\\mathrm{OR}(l, r)$$$ denotes $$$b_{l}$$$ $$$|$$$ $$$b_{l+1} $$$ $$$|$$$ $$$ \\ldots $$$ $$$|$$$ $$$ b_{r}$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1605F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1605/problem/F"}